--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Speech recognition
  This repository no longer builds or distributes a speech engine or model
  weights. The Windows bundle that did (whisper.cpp, MIT; ggml conversions of
  OpenAI Whisper weights, MIT) was removed on 2026-10-04; its pins, build
  recipe and notices are in the Git tag app-0.5-final. `sciwhisper-asr`
  calls a recogniser the user installed and does not download one.

Rust crates
  The workspace links around 170 third-party crates. Every one of them, with
  the licence it declares, is listed in packaging/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.json,
  which is generated from the lockfile and checked on every test run: a
  dependency that appears without a recorded licence, or under a licence this
  project has not reviewed, fails the build.

  All of them are permissive. At the time of writing none is under a licence
  whose notice must travel with a distribution (MPL-2.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0,
  BSL-1.0 on its own); the test `licences_that_require_a_notice_are_named_in_notice`
  fails if one appears without being named here.

  Nothing in the graph is under GPL, AGPL or an LGPL-only licence. One crate
  (`r-efi`) offers LGPL-2.1-or-later as one of three alternatives; this
  project takes the MIT option.

